            "tree_id": "e32cf1c6ce4a1a77d3e9bfa10278207716b2fcea",
            "message": "fix(static): apply the RFC 850 50-year rule to the full timestamp\n\nRFC 9110 reinterprets an RFC 850 date that is more than 50 years in the\nfuture, which is a comparison of the whole timestamp, not just the year.\nComparing years alone turned `15-Nov-76` into 2076 on 14 November 2026,\none day past the limit. The date is now built first and moved back a\ncentury only when it lands after now plus 50 years. Boundary tests cover\none day past the limit (1976) and exactly 50 years ahead (2076).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <redacted@example.invalid>",
            "timestamp": "2026-11-14T11:36:16Z",
